        rdfs:comment                   "Plain weave cotton embroidered with wool and silk in straight stitches.\nDirectional design with the top of the pattern at the bottom of the panel, so that the wearer saw the correct pattern.\nThere is a bottom border worked irregularly so that the upper edge is not a continuous straight line. The pattern of the bottom border is based on diagonal lines running from lower right to upper left. Each stripe is filled with a diaper  pattern  in one colour on the white cotton ground: blue, light brown, red, light brown, blue etc.. The embroidery stops before the top edge and the pattern in the top right hand part of the border is incomplete.\n\nThe pattern is a series of black diagonal lines from lower right to upper left.  \nThere are two sizes of stripes: \n[1] narrow stripes: light brown ground with a blue or red bud on a black stem with a triangular base.  These point downward in all except the lowest band on the left hand side.\n [2] wider stripe in two designs: [a] red ground with a sun-like flowerhead with either blue and light blue or green and yellow petals. [b] blue ground with a dark red tulip-like flower. \n\nThreads: Wool: blue, black, light brown, red; Z-spun.   Silk: yellow, pink, purple, light blue, light green, orange, 2S\nSee no. 52-1877"@en , "F, embroidered, 1830-1860, Persian"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/538574c5-125f-31e9-9ea3-952befd19cf9> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "F, embroidered, 1830-1860, Persian"@en , "Plain weave cotton embroidered with wool and silk in straight stitches.\nDirectional design with the top of the pattern at the bottom of the panel, so that the wearer saw the correct pattern.\nThere is a bottom border worked irregularly so that the upper edge is not a continuous straight line. The pattern of the bottom border is based on diagonal lines running from lower right to upper left. Each stripe is filled with a diaper  pattern  in one colour on the white cotton ground: blue, light brown, red, light brown, blue etc.. The embroidery stops before the top edge and the pattern in the top right hand part of the border is incomplete.\n\nThe pattern is a series of black diagonal lines from lower right to upper left.  \nThere are two sizes of stripes: \n[1] narrow stripes: light brown ground with a blue or red bud on a black stem with a triangular base.  These point downward in all except the lowest band on the left hand side.\n [2] wider stripe in two designs: [a] red ground with a sun-like flowerhead with either blue and light blue or green and yellow petals. [b] blue ground with a dark red tulip-like flower. \n\nThreads: Wool: blue, black, light brown, red; Z-spun.   Silk: yellow, pink, purple, light blue, light green, orange, 2S\nSee no. 52-1877"@en ;
